<title>USA: Supervalu Q1 earnings rise despite expenses.</title>
<headline>Supervalu Q1 earnings rise despite expenses.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Supervalu Inc, which earlier reported higher first-quarter earnings, said Thursday its results improved despite higher expenses for technology and the negative impact of an inventory accounting method.</p>
<p>Earlier, the food retailer and distributing company said its earnings rose eight percent to $49.8 million from $46.0 million a year ago. Earnings per share rose to a record $0.74 during the first quarter from $0.68 last year.</p>
</text>
